& [Correction] is material but compatible
  + Honesty guards semantic and epistemic identity boundaries including claim kind, source attribution, equivalence, contradiction, and uncertainty
  + Security guards operational identity boundaries including principal, authority, subject scope, resource, disclosure, mutation, and effect
  + both guardians establish the admissible boundary before combinatory projection and validate that boundary after a candidate next step is refined
  + Weaver projects relational combinatory potential as compatible composites, decompositions, seam alternatives, and incompatibilities
  + Planner projects temporal combinatory potential as reachable sequences, prerequisites, branches, checkpoints, stops, and counterfactual paths
  + projection does not admit, authorize, execute, or inscribe a candidate

& [RevisedCycle] is boundary, potential, selection, and inscription
  + Observer binds subject and purpose
  + Scribe anchors exact entry state
  + Honesty and Security establish guarded identity boundaries
  + Weaver and Planner project relational and temporal combinatory potential inside those boundaries
  + Refiner forms the smallest supported candidate step from that potential
  + Honesty and Security validate boundary preservation and admissibility
  + Observer decides the disposition
  + Scribe inscribes the typed result and residual frontier

& [DataCorrection] is bounded
  + add FacultyStage bound and project
  + replace Weaver compose stage with Weaver project stage
  + replace Planner plan stage with Planner project stage
  + require Honesty and Security bound activations before projection and final gate activations after refinement
  + retain faculty-specific purpose and ledger so the two project stages remain distinguishable
  + retain the same FacultyCycle and SemanticTransition waist

& [CompatibilityReview] passes
  + SAIL already supplies BOUND, COMPOSE, DECOMPOSE, SEQUENCE, FORK, CHOOSE, GATE, and VALIDATE primitives
  + faculty programs remain compiled libraries above those primitives
  + existing Honesty, Security, Planner, and Weaver contracts support the sharpened interpretation
  + no new effect or provider authority is introduced
  + no source revision beyond this preserved clarification is required

